{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385544-alternative-settings-and-v5","id":1385544,"title":"Alternative Settings and V5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-03T22:53:21-07:00","id":1385544,"title":"Alternative Settings and V5","content":"Over the decades, my Vampire group and I very frequently used alternative V:tM settings. Tzimisce and/or Lasombra in the Camarilla, some Clans don't exist or some Bloodlines are Cans, etc. We used to get threads about that kind of stuff rarely often. Now that V5 is out, I see fewer threads on such topics and I find myself less able to get interested in V5 because it assumes a Revised canon which I seldom used.<br /> <br /> Is there anybody else who used non-canon settings and have you been able to adapt V5 or any of the fluff from it into your setting(s)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T22:57:56-07:00","id":1385546,"title":"","content":"I once did a campaign where the DC Universe and V:TM were merged.<br /> <br /> I used Mithras the basis for Kal-El, Prince of Metropolis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T03:17:03-07:00","id":1385569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385544-alternative-settings-and-v5#post1385544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that V5 is out, I see fewer threads on such topics and I find myself less able to get interested in V5 because it assumes a Revised canon which I seldom used.</div> </div> </div> </div>lol, what?<br /> I suggest you re-read V5, cause there's hardly any trace from Revised<br /> <br /> and, the reason there's few threads on the subject (well, &quot;few&quot; by your standards) is because you need a &quot;setting&quot; before you can make an &quot;alternate&quot; setting<br /> <br /> right now, despite having two sectbooks, it still feels like there's huge gaps to be filled,<br /> at this point, such discussions would be less about alternate settings and more about expanded universes<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T06:05:47-07:00","id":1385595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385544-alternative-settings-and-v5?p=1385569#post1385569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> lol, what?<br /> I suggest you re-read V5, cause there's hardly any trace from Revised<br /> <br /> and, the reason there's few threads on the subject (well, &quot;few&quot; by your standards) is because you need a &quot;setting&quot; before you can make an &quot;alternate&quot; setting<br /> <br /> right now, despite having two sectbooks, it still feels like there's huge gaps to be filled,<br /> at this point, such discussions would be less about alternate settings and more about expanded universes</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit of threadcrapping, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T06:17:05-07:00","id":1385596,"title":"","content":"Some interesting bits here that I've experimented with:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>The DC World of Darkness</b>: &quot;Superheroes with fangs&quot; is taken literally as the majority of cities are ruled by Princes who are adapted characters from DC comics. Kal-El of the lost Kryptonian people is the 4th generation Ventrue Prince of Metropolis, Batman is the Old Clan Tzimisce Prince of Gotham against a perpetual Sabbat siege, and Diana Prince is a Amazon 5th generation Ventrue. They have all served as Justicars for the Camarilla and represent the American Ivory Tower's best. However, the worst of the Camarilla and Sabbat undermine them every day while questions become if they should form their own organization. It's a flashier, more cinematic universe with the Masquerade hanging by a thread.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Marvel Comics World of Darkness</b>: I use Mage: The Ascension here as the Technocracy hides behind organizations like SHIELD to carry out their pogrom of Mutants [Hedge Mages, Mages, and Orphans] with HIT Mark Sentinels. The Technocracy/Tradition/Nephandi alliance of WW2 also continues as Hydra. New York City is ruled by the Syndicate Kingpin and he'll let Outcast Mages survive as long as they work for him while those who fight against him will end up falling prey to his mercenaries.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Open World of Darkness</b>: Basically, like True Blood, the vampires now live in the open of the world as do other supernaturals. They've managed to pull the wool over the eyes of most people and live as the rich 1% (or at least the Ivory Tower does). The Anarchs struggle against the twin forces of human bigotry as well as the fact the Camarilla would like to purge a majority of new Embraces as they are harder to cover up for. Werewolves HATE this situation and are actively working against it. The Union is, meanwhile, crumbling behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Second Inquisition Triumphant</b>: Half of the vampire race has been exterminated by the Second Inquisition, which is secretly bankrolled by the Technocracy, with no hint of it stopping. Some cities have managed to become sanctuaries for the undead but hundreds of them have been purged like London. Anarch or Camarilla doesn't matter as the factions have been forced on the backfoot repeatedly. Any vampire that is discovered potentially threatens them all as he'll name every name he can to save his own life once captured. The Masquerade is paramount but so, perhaps, is acceptance or fighting until the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T09:28:05-07:00","id":1385611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385544-alternative-settings-and-v5?p=1385569#post1385569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> lol, what?<br /> I suggest you re-read V5, cause there's hardly any trace from Revised<br /> <br /> and, the reason there's few threads on the subject (well, &quot;few&quot; by your standards) is because you need a &quot;setting&quot; before you can make an &quot;alternate&quot; setting<br /> <br /> right now, despite having two sectbooks, it still feels like there's huge gaps to be filled,<br /> at this point, such discussions would be less about alternate settings and more about expanded universes</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, no. Everything is an advancement from Revised, told in broad strokes in the core, advanced by 14 years of metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T10:18:33-07:00","id":1385616,"title":"","content":"I think that non-cannon has somewhat became the cannon of VtM. In previous editions we always had our own take on the WoD and this was, as the OP put it in all the threads. Everyone played by there on house rules and we all had little quirks in the story that made our individual chronicles unique. I don't thing that V5 has changed this. I actually believe that it has embraced that by pushing the concept of unreliable narrator even further.<br /> <br /> What I do see is less of a willingness to engage in the imagination and break with the established rules. It seems that more people take the rules as unbendable or breakable or even changeable.<br /> <br /> I for one love saying the week of nightmares does not exist and way before V5 played that, as was hinted, Gehenna was cyclical. I was not a fan of the destruction of the Shadowlands so I typically say that didn't happen and since that did not happen neither did the Avatar storm. Though I now play with the malady in many of my games and spirits are a bit more hostile because Gia is pulling away for the world, but that is due to recent things I have read. not much of this besides the Shadowlands being business as usual really effects my Vampire games but one that does is the 1 edition notion that there are more than 13 clans.<br /> <br /> basically their may be more clans than the 13. in 1st edition there was more than 13 then it got pulled back to 13 in 2nd and then it was their might be more in revised and now in 5th I think we may see us going back to 1st where their are more than 13 which is fine by me. I don't have the cain myth being the truth behind vampire origins only the vampires beleive this and onlder vampires no it is not true but like the masses in an easily contained box. Set taught that Vampires did not descend from cain and that we could be more as we are gods made flesh and that caused all sorts of trouble so those kind of thoughts need to be quelled. The book of nod hints that there was more to Caine being the first and the revelations of the dark mother almost flat out tell the truth so these books are heresy. I think this is the main change for my world.<br /> <br /> I may not like all the books in every edition but I do read them to inspire my story and Cannon is what the ST at the table sets not what the authors write cause since this game began they change there minds quite often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T12:02:13-07:00","id":1385633,"title":"","content":"When I first started creating my own version of the Setting for my chronicles (in late 2nd edition/early Revised), it was recognizably Vampire with only a few changes. However, with the increasing metaplot, it'd probably now be an &quot;Alternative&quot; take since the changes are no longer minor. Not because I kept making changes, but because the Developers kept making changes - and then changes to those changes and so on.<br /> <br /> Personally I think this metaplot route in a mistake. It needlessly drives players/customers away from the game by introducing controversies.<br /> <br /> I think a better route would have been for the Developers to introduce their ideas not as metaplot across the entire game world, but by sourcebook scenarios and settng books that would introduce one element and allow the STs to develop that however they see fit. So if you want a badass Inquisition that presents a real threat, create a new By Night book with a compelling setting and make the Inquisition the big chronicle tentpole instead of yet another Methusaleh secretly living in the city. If you want a badass Sabbat Crusade that throws the Camarilla on its news, create a new By Night book of a Camarilla city and then include lots of Sabbat NPCs and explain how the Sabbat Crusade should unfold during the chronicle. <br /> <br /> You could take almost any controversial element in the last 20+ years, and if you only used it as a showcase element in ONE By Night book, it wouldn't create any problems and probably be embraced in some form by almost every ST. Make them toolkits that allow each ST to decide what to use in their own games. You could get all the benefits of &quot;moving the game forward&quot; yet not cock up the setting and alienate fans.<br /> <br /> I know that the refrain is that the By Night books didn't sell well relative to the others. But there is a reason for that. Outside a few classics, they just were not that good. I remember the early days when every new release was easily sought out. The problem wasn't that it was a By Night book, but that they were done so poorly that players began associating them with low quality crap. (And a frequent complaint that was that every city was about a secret Methusaleh - but if you do something else with it, then all of a sudden that complaint went away).<br /> <br /> In terms of fluff from V5 I might use, it's probably none. But I do admit that some ideas I find intriguing, and some ideas &quot;new&quot; to V5 are things I actually introduced into my own chronicle setting long ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T16:47:24-07:00","id":1385677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385544-alternative-settings-and-v5?p=1385596#post1385596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. <b>Second Inquisition Triumphant</b>...</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be an interesting setting. It would be more interesting to cross the scenarios - the world knows about monsters, and the world hates monsters. The end of the world is a process, not an event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}